From 2f9d4bb1a87e4e95b8dc89b76e55ad3267092645 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pkgdemon <jpm820@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:53:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] devfs: route EVFILT_VNODE on device files to the vnode layer

devfs_kqfilter_f() handed every kqueue registration on a device file to
the driver's d_kqfilter.  Drivers implement only data filters such as
EVFILT_READ/EVFILT_WRITE (ttydev_kqfilter returns EINVAL for anything
else), so EVFILT_VNODE on a device fd failed with EINVAL, even though
the vnode layer (vfs_kqfilter) supports it and devfs vnodes post
NOTE_REVOKE from vop_reclaim_post when they are revoked or their cdev
is destroyed.  This behaviour is inherited from FreeBSD.

On NextBSD, follow Darwin: EVFILT_VNODE describes the file, so send it
to VOP_KQFILTER(fp->f_vnode), as vn_kqfilter does for regular files.
All other filters still go to the driver.  The registration still runs
under devfs_fp_check(), so a device that is already gone returns ENXIO
as before.  The knote holds the vnode via vhold() and is released by
filt_vfsdetach(); it takes no cdev reference, so the dev_relthread()
pairing is unchanged.

This lets Apple's launchd arm EVFILT_VNODE/NOTE_REVOKE on its
/dev/console fd unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/fs/devfs/devfs_vnops.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sys/fs/devfs/devfs_vnops.c b/sys/fs/devfs/devfs_vnops.c
index 8c188e7..0f7ec96 100644
--- a/sys/fs/devfs/devfs_vnops.c
+++ b/sys/fs/devfs/devfs_vnops.c
@@ -1014,7 +1014,20 @@ devfs_kqfilter_f(struct file *fp, struct knote *kn)
 	error = devfs_fp_check(fp, &dev, &dsw, &ref);
 	if (error)
 		return (error);
-	error = dsw->d_kqfilter(dev, kn);
+	/*
+	 * NextBSD: EVFILT_VNODE describes the file, not the device, so
+	 * route it to the vnode layer as for regular files (vn_kqfilter)
+	 * rather than to the driver, which only knows READ/WRITE-style
+	 * filters.  This matches Darwin, where device files support
+	 * EVFILT_VNODE (e.g. NOTE_REVOKE on a revoked or destroyed tty).
+	 * The knote holds the vnode (vhold) and is detached through
+	 * filt_vfsdetach; it takes no cdev reference, so the thread
+	 * reference from devfs_fp_check is dropped as usual below.
+	 */
+	if (kn->kn_filter == EVFILT_VNODE)
+		error = VOP_KQFILTER(fp->f_vnode, kn);
+	else
+		error = dsw->d_kqfilter(dev, kn);
 	td->td_fpop = fpop;
 	dev_relthread(dev, ref);
 	return (error);
